  "_about": {
    "purpose": "English jarh-wa-ta'dil grade tokens -> their established Urdu/Arabic-script equivalents, for the narrator bio sheet.",
    "why_a_glossary": "These are technical verdicts on a narrator's reliability drawn from a closed vocabulary, not prose. Across all 6,641 bundled narrators there are only 218 distinct tokens, and the 11 commonest account for the large majority. Mapping the settled terms is exact and reviewable; free machine translation of a scholarly verdict is not, and a shifted word changes the ruling.",
    "scope": "Only terms with a settled equivalent in Urdu rijal literature are listed. Anything absent stays in English and the narrator keeps gradeNeedsUrdu = true, so a gap reads as a gap.",
    "verified_prefix": "The source renders a confirmed grade as 'verified X'. The prefix is a display marker, not part of the verdict, so 'verified X' maps to the same term as 'X'.",
    "review_state": "machine_provisional — mapped by terminology table, not yet checked by a qualified reviewer. Gate public release on that review."
